摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH Web GUI right sidebar: VS Code-style file explorer plus source control (git status, stage/unstage/discard, commit, diff, commit graph, sync fetch/pull/push, branch/remote management, git init, multi-repo, color-coded file status, file-type icons, image preview) with editable ","id":"gh:1343301031","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-solution-explorer","slug":"xiaoksio/dsh-solution-explorer","topics":["code-editor","deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","developer-tools","diff-viewer","dsh-plugin","file-explorer","git","git-gui","sidebar","source-control"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH Web GUI right sidebar: VS Code-style file explorer plus source control (git status, stage/unstag"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"e/discard, commit, diff, commit graph, sync fetch/pull/push, branch/remote management, git init, mul"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"ti-repo, color-coded file status, file-type icons, image preview) with editable "},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# 🗂️ Solution Explorer for DSH"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**A drop-in replacement for the DSH Web GUI's right sidebar** — VS Code-style file explorer, a multi"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"-tab editor with in-place previews, and full source control."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- **Takes over the sidebar** — every file opened from the conversation, the\nsidebar's own file list "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"or source control lands in this plugin's editor view:\nas long as this plugin can read a file, the sh"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"ipped preview panel never takes\nit over.\n- **File Explorer** — browse the current session workspace "},{"id":"p6s4","text":"as a directory tree\nwith expand/collapse, VS Code-style file-type icons (TS/JS/Vue/JSON/image/\narchi"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"ve/script and 30+ more extensions), git status markers (M/A/D/R/?), names\ncolor-coded by status (gre"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"en untracked / yellow modified / grey ignored),\n`.gitignore`-excluded files and folders shown grey, "},{"id":"p6s7","text":"and directory \"modified\"\nindicators.\n- **Source Control** — staged / unstaged / untracked change lis"},{"id":"p6s8","text":"ts with\nstage / unstage / discard (per-file or all), commit with a message, and a\nbranch info bar. *"},{"id":"p6s9","text":"*AI commit message**: pick a host-configured model in\nSettings and tap the ✨-icon beside the commit "},{"id":"p6s10","text":"box to generate a Conventional\nCommits draft from the staged diff (optionally guided by the repo's\nA"},{"id":"p6s11","text":"GENTS.md). **Diff view**: full-file side-by-side compare with an\neditable right column (Enter splits"},{"id":"p6s12","text":" lines, backspace/delete merges, NBSP\nplaceholders), a middle gutter to stage (⤒) or revert (↩) indi"},{"id":"p6s13","text":"vidual hunks,\nCtrl+S to save. **Commit Graph**: an SVG history view with\nbranch lanes and merge line"},{"id":"p6s14","text":"s; click a commit to expand its changed files\n(with file-type icons and status letters M/A/D/R) belo"},{"id":"p6s15","text":"w the row, hover for\na tooltip with the full message, stats, and a GitHub link; plus checkout. **Syn"},{"id":"p6s16","text":"c**: fetch / pull / push / sync (pull +\npush) with ahead/behind counts, each remote-write confirmed."},{"id":"p6s17","text":" **Branches**:\nswitch / create / rename / delete / merge / publish. **Remotes**: add /\nremove / set "},{"id":"p6s18","text":"URL. **Git Init**: initialize a repository from a plain\ndirectory. **Merge changes**: pull/merge con"},{"id":"p6s19","text":"flicts (UU/AA/DD/…) are\ndetected and listed for manual resolution. **Multi-repo support**:\nauto-disc"},{"id":"p6s20","text":"overs git repositories under the workspace and lets you switch\nbetween them; the SCM panel follows t"},{"id":"p6s21","text":"he selected repo. **Split panes**: drag\nthe divider between changes and repository to resize, histor"},{"id":"p6s22","text":"y fills the\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Screenshots"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| File Explorer | Source Control | Diff |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"> [!WARNING]\n> This is a third-party community plugin. Installing it runs its code on your\n> machine"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" with your own permissions. It can read, modify, and delete files and\n> run git operations (includin"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"g destructive ones such as discard and delete)\n> inside your session workspace. Review the source be"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"fore use and back up\n> important work first. You are responsible for what this plugin does with your"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"k up\n> important work first. You are responsible for what this plugin does with your\n> repositories."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### From dsh-market (GUI)"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Open the marketplace in the DSH Web UI, search for \"solution-explorer\", and\nclick install."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### From npm"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### From a local checkout"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"After installing, reload the Web UI. The explorer panel appears as its own right\ncolumn once a sessi"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"on with a workspace is active."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- **DSH 0.1.x / 0.2.x** — the declared peer range is\n`>=0.1.0-rc.1 <0.3.0-0` (tested from `0.1.5-rc."},{"id":"p19s2","text":"1`, including `0.2.0-rc.2`).\n- **Minimum plugin version per DSH release**:\n- DSH ≥ 0.1.7: **1.0.1** "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"— from 0.1.7 the Session-list snapshot no longer carries\n`current` (the main-view Session is the one"},{"id":"p19s4","text":" retained by `mainView`), and an older\nplugin hides the whole right column because of it (#2).\n- DSH"},{"id":"p19s5","text":" ≥ 0.2.0: **1.0.2** — 0.2 renamed the official icon exports from\n`IconXxx16`/`IconXxx14` to `IconXxx"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"Regular`/`IconXxxMedium`; the old names resolve\nto `undefined`, React throws #130, and the panel ren"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"ders as an empty column (#3).\n- DSH validates these peer ranges before installing or activating a pl"},{"id":"p19s8","text":"ugin, so a\nplugin older than the installed DSH is refused at install time rather than\nfailing at run"},{"id":"p19s9","text":"time. After upgrading DSH, check this plugin's version in the\nsettings page before assuming the pane"},{"id":"p19s10","text":"ter upgrading DSH, check this plugin's version in the\nsettings page before assuming the panel broke."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The plugin accepts an optional `config` in the bundle row\n(`cordis.patch.yml`):"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Field | Type | Default | Description |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| `defaultWidth` | `number` | `280` | Panel width in px, clamped to 264–560. |\n| `autoOpen` | `boole"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"an` | `true` | Auto-open the panel when a session activates. |\n| `filterPatterns` | `string[]` | `[]"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"` | Name patterns to hide from the file tree. |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The plugin is a single npm package with two halves, both declared in\n`package.json` under the `dsh` "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"plugin is a single npm package with two halves, both declared in\n`package.json` under the `dsh` key:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- **Host half** (`src/index.ts`, exports `.` → `lib/index.js`): runs in the\ndsh host process and ser"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"ves the workspace-gated filesystem and git API over\nHTTP routes under `/solution-explorer/*` (`tree`"},{"id":"p26s3","text":", `read`, `write`,\n`delete`, `search`, `git-repos`, `git-status`, `git-diff`, `git-log`,\n`git-stage`"},{"id":"p26s4","text":", `git-unstage`, `git-discard`, `git-commit`, `paste`, `move`,\n`upload`, `create`). All routes\nresol"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"ve paths strictly inside the session workspace root. It also announces\nitself in the system prompt s"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"o the agent knows what the panel can do.\n- **Browser half** (`src/client/index.ts`, exports `./clien"},{"id":"p26s7","text":"t` →\n`lib/client.js`): loaded by the Web GUI's `__ModuleLoader__` as a\nclosure-factory bundle. It ap"},{"id":"p26s8","text":"pends the explorer column to the frame grid\n(`[data-dsh-frame]`), follows the active session's `cwd`"},{"id":"p26s9","text":", and mounts the\nfile editor into the `conversation.view` slot. A `sidebarRightTabs`\nregistration cl"},{"id":"p26s10","text":"aims every `dsh-resource://file/**` address, so a file opened\nanywhere in the GUI is handed to that "},{"id":"p26s11","text":"editor view instead of the shipped\npreview panel."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
